Comment (frontend/src/App.vue:231):
`setError` overwrites the session-expired message set in `handleUnauthorized()` because API requests call `onUnauthorized()` on 401 and then throw, and the catch blocks call `setError(...)` which replaces `errorMessage`. Consider detecting `ApiError` with `status === 401` here and returning early (or preserving the existing `errorMessage`) so the user consistently sees the session-expired prompt.

---
Comment (frontend/src/App.vue:275):
This status/error banner always uses `role="status"`, even when displaying an error. For accessibility, errors should typically use `role="alert"` (assertive) while non-error updates can remain `status`/polite; consider switching the role (and/or `aria-live`) based on whether `errorMessage` is set.

---
Comment (frontend/src/App.vue:117):
`createTodo()` trims the title/description but does not validate the trimmed values before sending. A whitespace-only title will become an empty string and will be rejected by the backend (title has `min=1` validation), resulting in a avoidable 400. Consider validating after `trim()` and showing a client-side message instead of making the request.

---
Comment (frontend/src/App.vue:149):
`saveTodo()` trims the edited title/description but does not validate the trimmed title before calling the API. If a user enters only whitespace, this will send an empty title and the backend will reject it (`min=1`), leaving the UI in edit mode with an error. Consider validating trimmed inputs and preventing the request when invalid.

---
Comment (frontend/src/App.vue:93):
`submitAuth()` sends `authForm.username`/`password` as-is. This allows leading/trailing whitespace (e.g., usernames that visually match but fail backend validation). Consider trimming `username` (and possibly rejecting whitespace-only values) before calling `register`/`login` to match backend expectations (`min=3` for register).

